complete and perfect even to the point of duplicating magical abilities and even the latent sapience in some of those swords that have almost a mind of their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anybody else got some fictional characters that might be interesting if it turned out their lives were Keeper's game?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually yeah, that sounds...<br /> <br /> Familiar. Wasn't this the basic idea of something on fanfiction.net?<br /> <br /> [Checks]<br /> <br /> Actually yes it was. Liked it, only a couple chapters though. Pity, the idea of them slowly realizing their entire world was a bad, hyper-cynical True Fae imitation of the real one looked like it could have been interesting. Oh well, though I found it hilarious that the nWoD is actually, cosmologically speaking, a more fundamentally optimistic and life-affirming universe (for instance, our &quot;Dead Apostles&quot; are more selfish-by-necessity and desperately trying to ignore what they are rather than the undead scourges of humanity born from the world's autoimmune disorder with a side business in Slaanesh worship). One wondered what the Keeper's actual identity would be (Angra Maniyu with the Grail as his Prop form, most likely, but I'm not putting Gaia out of the running)<br /> <br /> You the author, or just cribbing an idea? Either's fine (I crib all the time), but...<br /> <br /> As for me, I can see the backstory of Requiem vampires involving Gaia being betrayed when asking the Ultimate Ones for help in destroying humanity; rather than Brunestud answering, it was the Strix. The Strix, of course, don't give a damn about any higher ideology than libertine aspirations, and started experimenting with humans to make them more like themselves. They hate humanity, but only for being something they find strange and alien (empathy, restraint, kindness-what are these emotions, and why do they give humans happiness?). The actual Ultimate One who did answer, Idmun Luduth, is actually rather fond of humans and wishes simply that they find a balance with nature, returning the world to an unspoiled state is not on his/her agenda at all.<br /> <br /> Not related to changelings directly, but thanks to bloodroot that idea can be introduced by interacting with the Kindred, either as theory or truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T13:40:00-07:00","id":279030,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wrote that. Unfortunately for my fanfiction, most of my writing time goes toward my original fiction these days. That was just sort of quickly written off because the idea struck me and I wanted to at least get a chapter out. The longer version you suggest sounds a better story, but not one I likely have time for at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T13:45:51-07:00","id":279039,"title":"","content":"In sense of a loose nod, I had Gaia responsible for creation of Gangrel progenitor, but that's because she believes strongly in the survival of the strongest as the guiding principle in how species should evolve, and thus she constantly challenges her children. In a world full of danger, supernatural and mundane, humans are more pressed to develop such traits that increase their collective survival as the species. Including tools and technology to fend off the predators, as anything steming from human ingenuity is valid for her. Also, the weakness to sunlight and fire with which Gangrel are burdened makes it more challenging for them to prey on humans. If she &quot;blesses&quot; someone, it always comes with more burden to overcome than benefits. She was actually amused how the first Gangrel struggled with the Beast and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Unlike Nasuverse Gaia, she actually is fond of humans (in a twisted way), but like a mother that wants best for her children she exposes them to hardships so they get stronger.<br /> <br /> PS. Other Kindred Clan have different origins than Gangrel, I but I haven't figured out yet how they came to be in my personal mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-12-2014, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T22:55:46-07:00","id":279392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_cont